{"name":"Flamingo Feather","hex":"#f8bdd9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flamingo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wading bird of the family Phoenicopteridae of the order Phoenicopteriformes.","A deep pink color tinged with orange, like that of a flamingo."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep pink color tinged with orange, like that of a flamingo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flamingo"},{"term":"feather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A branching, hair-like structure that grows on the bodies of birds, used for flight, swimming, protection and display.","Long hair on the lower legs of a dog or horse, especially a draft horse, notably the Clydesdale breed. Narrowly only the rear hair."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or furnish with feathers;  to fletch.","To adorn, as if with feathers; to fringe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laurens van der Post","blocks":[{"text":"Sir Laurens Jan van der Post,, was a South African Afrikaner writer, farmer, soldier, educator, journalist, humanitarian, philosopher, explorer and conservationist. He was noted for his interest in Jungianism and the Kalahari Bushmen, his experiences during World War II, as well as his relationships with notable figures such as King Charles III and British Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher. After his death, there was controversy over claims that he had exaggerated many aspects of his life, as well the revelation that he had impregnated a 14-year-old girl entrusted to his care."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Sir_Laurens_van_Der_Post_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurens_van_der_Post"},{"title":"Flamingo","blocks":[{"text":"Flamingos or flamingoes are a type of wading bird in the family Phoenicopteridae, which is the only 